  "title": "Vertex Cover Integrality Gap",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there is $\\delta > 0$ such that, for every large $n$, there are $n$-vertex graphs $G$ and $H$ such that $G \\equiv_{\\delta n}^{\\mathrm{C}} H$ and $\\mathrm{vc}(G) \\ge (2 - \\varepsilon) \\cdot \\mathrm{vc}(H)$.",
